ratorname{sin}⁡(8x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x) & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8x+3x)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8x-3x)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(11x)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(8x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(11x)+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{22}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(11x)-\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-340479/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9d3b7f35-fcd1-5443-b0ea-0b06e016e0c3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-340479"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-340483/selection/8f912eaafa64274cf6d709bd0c2852ac2d3c90b91d76fe03c7e9d9e299a08662" :answer/id #uuid "f28ce658-1195-57f7-8bde-b60d8abf3d67" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{24}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340483/selection/996c13bd191b9146364355a522c6919429c5a7f07e7d3e59e8b48e34c7042e44" :answer/id #uuid "8daa46b2-5323-58b0-a420-761f3efb2179" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{24}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(12x)+\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340483/selection/ae59d204fbc708d614bec5d4e42171d6197dffede7af8e9e702df6c8ee02594c" :answer/id #uuid "815b0c61-439a-5054-89dd-76ead181b0e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)+\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340483/selection/22db19e41e07ec3dd454750f11878b1a84c2b22ae7ffa40d737e42a2288b6539" :answer/id #uuid "0422f2eb-7f61-5e23-bd00-f566513e6b69" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{12}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(12x)-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340483/selection/6e3ff088c1744a8a023b33c0e6edfa1706d545054ef4c9421b199b6ed6e9116a" :answer/id #uuid "09d2d64b-31b4-5e58-b3b2-f6b0ae12a527" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{24}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(12x)-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340483/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "dcc00f90-f685-5365-b535-2af958bcdb13" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-340483/selection/6e3ff088c1744a8a023b33c0e6edfa1706d545054ef4c9421b199b6ed6e9116a" :answer-field/choices ["q-340483/selection/8f912eaafa64274cf6d709bd0c2852ac2d3c90b91d76fe03c7e9d9e299a08662" "q-340483/selection/996c13bd191b9146364355a522c6919429c5a7f07e7d3e59e8b48e34c7042e44" "q-340483/selection/ae59d204fbc708d614bec5d4e42171d6197dffede7af8e9e702df6c8ee02594c" "q-340483/selection/22db19e41e07ec3dd454750f11878b1a84c2b22ae7ffa40d737e42a2288b6539" "q-340483/selection/6e3ff088c1744a8a023b33c0e6edfa1706d545054ef4c9421b199b6ed6e9116a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-340483" :question/id #uuid "a135a1df-aa0e-5ea6-9580-c700cdbdf03a" :question/math-academy-id "q-340483" :question/problem "$\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the sum and difference formulas for sine:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\alpha +\\beta ) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta +\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\beta  \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\alpha -\\beta ) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta -\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\beta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding these equations, we get the following product-to-sum identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\alpha +\\beta )+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\alpha -\\beta ) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta  \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\alpha +\\beta )+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\alpha -\\beta ))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x) & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x+5x)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x-5x)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(12x)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(12x)+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{24}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(12x)-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-340483/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9d3b7f35-fcd1-5443-b0ea-0b06e016e0c3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-340483"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-340505/field-1/ffd11cf0cc7fc42dd49240fe2a8f399d54da15e1798557ceab1ff4e29e1b34eb" :answer/id #uuid "6e2c3ce8-147a-54d0-9b78-d30c68e2288b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8}{55}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340505/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "6effd691-5287-5b89-9f0d-92c8725847d1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-340505/field-1/ffd11cf0cc7fc42dd49240fe2a8f399d54da15e1798557ceab1ff4e29e1b34eb" :answer-field/choices ["q-340505/field-1/ffd11cf0cc7fc42dd49240fe2a8f399d54da15e1798557ceab1ff4e29e1b34eb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-340505" :question/id #uuid "cb756ef7-080e-5245-8c3b-08721c6ba08e" :question/math-academy-id "q-340505" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8x)\\,\\text{d}x=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the sum and difference formulas for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\alpha -\\beta ) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\beta  \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\alpha +\\beta ) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\beta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubtracting the second equation from the first, we get the following product-to-sum identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\alpha -\\beta )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\alpha +\\beta ) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\beta  \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\beta  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\alpha -\\beta )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\alpha +\\beta ))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8x) & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x-8x)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x+8x)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-5x)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(11x)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(11x)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(11x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)-\\frac{1}{22}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(11x)]}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0))-\\frac{1}{22}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{11\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}(1-0)-\\frac{1}{22}(-1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{55}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-340505/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8a371de4-7c3f-5687-bd3a-d3ab5ab803ce"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-340505"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
